or parents of New Jersey (or any other state), this is the best argument for homeschooling or private schools. \nMy story.  When I became a teacher in California in 1999, I had to take this test.  It was scheduled well in advance, and the military had other plans.  I was deployed with my troops for 30 days. I didn't even have time to review the test study materials.  I arrived home at 3:00 AM, and the test was at 7:30 AM.  I took a quick shower and drove to the test site.  Several hundred people gathered at the test site.  I and another older gentleman stood around, listening to how many had failed multiple times.  We looked at each other with dread and shrugged our shoulders. We were both assigned to the same classroom and sat in the same row. The proctor asked how many were retaking the test and/or a portion of the test.  75+%  raised their hands.  He and I looked at each other and shrugged again.  We were informed of the rules and the time (four hrs for all testers) and were told to begin. We were the first two done (just under 90 minutes). As we were walking out, we realized that if you couldn't pass the test, you shouldn't be a teacher.  It was possibly the most straightforward test I had ever taken, and it required basic math and reading comprehension skills.", 'entity_set': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': []}, 'richtext': {'richtext_tags': [{'from_index': 0, 'to_index': 111, 'richtext_types': ['Bold', 'Italic']}]}, 'media': {'inline_media': []}}}}, 'legacy': {'bookmark_count': 0, 'bookmarked': False, 'created_at': 'Mon Jan 06 16:18:56 +0000 2025', 'conversation_id_str': '1875914242689290528', 'display_text_range': [14, 294], 'entities': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'timestamps': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': [{'id_str': '69156861', 'name': 'Chief Nerd', 'screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'indices': [0, 13]}]}, 'favorite_count': 2, 'favorited': False, 'full_text': '@TheChiefNerd For parents of New Jersey (or any other state), thi